{
  "tanrei": {
    "comp": {
      "button": {
        "$extensions": {
          "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
            "rationale": "One product uses buttons at several emphasis levels and several sizes, enabled and disabled: with a label, with an icon beside the label, or with an icon alone (in toolbars, rows and cards), some of them switches that are on or off, and some of them actions that delete or discard something, which a person should be able to tell apart before pressing.",
            "since": "0.1.0"
          },
          "dev.tanrei.states": {
            "variants": [
              "filled",
              "tonal",
              "elevated",
              "outlined",
              "text"
            ],
            "states": [
              "hovered",
              "focused",
              "pressed",
              "disabled"
            ],
            "perVariant": {
              "container.color": "color",
              "label.color": "color",
              "icon.color": "color",
              "outline.color": "color",
              "state-layer.color": "color",
              "container.elevation": "shadow",
              "unselected.container.color": "color",
              "unselected.label.color": "color",
              "unselected.icon.color": "color",
              "unselected.outline.color": "color",
              "unselected.state-layer.color": "color",
              "selected.container.color": "color",
              "selected.label.color": "color",
              "selected.icon.color": "color",
              "selected.outline.color": "color",
              "selected.state-layer.color": "color",
              "destructive.container.color": "color",
              "destructive.label.color": "color",
              "destructive.icon.color": "color",
              "destructive.outline.color": "color",
              "destructive.state-layer.color": "color"
            },
            "perComponent": {
              "opacity": "number",
              "container.shape": "dimension"
            }
          },
          "dev.tanrei.llm": {
            "usage": "Everything a Button reads, and nothing else: size-dependent geometry (height, directional padding with and without an icon at either side, gap, and the narrow inset and the wide width of an icon-only button), its text style, its glyph sizes (beside a label, and alone), and for each variant (filled, tonal, elevated, outlined, text) the container / label / icon / outline colors and elevation of a plain button, of a toggle that is off (unselected.), of a toggle that is on (selected.) and of an action that deletes or discards (destructive.), in each state (resting, hovered, focused, pressed, disabled), plus per-state shape and opacity.",
            "rules": [
              "To restyle buttons in a product, change these tokens in a layer; never fork the component or add a variant.",
              "State tokens are valued by the design system's pattern rules (tanrei.comp.*.*.hovered.container.color …). Override one token, or replace the rule to change every component at once.",
              "A state that should look like rest aliases the resting token; a system that dims on press sets pressed.opacity.",
              "Heights are minimums: a height must hold 2 × padding-block + one label line, and the build reports it when it does not.",
              "label.color is the color of the label and of an icon beside it; icon.color is the color of the glyph of a button that has no label. Keep them equal unless an icon alone should be quieter or louder than a labelled action.",
              "An icon-only button is as wide as it is high by default, so container.shape draws a circle at corner.full and a rounded square at a smaller corner; its width prop sets the glyph between container.padding-inline-narrow, or draws container.width-wide, instead, for a tight row or a wider target. There is no token for the default width (it is the height) and none for the narrow one (it is the glyph and the inset twice).",
              "A toggle that is off must look quieter than one that is on; do not make unselected and selected the same.",
              "Each look's state-layer.color is the color hover, focus and press mix into its container; it aliases that look's label color.",
              "padding-inline-start-with-icon and padding-inline-end-with-icon are the padding on the side an icon sits at; keep them a step tighter than the plain paddings, because a glyph carries empty space inside its box that a label does not.",
              "destructive. is the look of an action that deletes or discards something, in each variant: the error role at the variant's own emphasis (filled: error and on-error; tonal: error-container and on-error-container; elevated, outlined and text: the error color on the variant's own container, and an outlined button's edge in it too). Disabled, it looks like any disabled button of its variant. A toggle has no destructive look.",
              "tone.container.opacity is how strongly a Button shows its container on a colored surface its host draws (BTN-45): the host gives the surface's content color, and the Button draws its label, icon and state layer in it, its container in it at this opacity, and hover, focus and press over that at sys.state's state-layer opacities. A host chooses the tone; a product never gives one."
            ]
          },
          "dev.tanrei.axes": {
            "size": {
              "default": "medium",
              "values": [
                "small",
                "medium",
                "large"
              ],
              "members": [
                "container.height",
                "container.padding-inline-narrow",
                "container.width-wide",
                "container.padding-inline-start",
                "container.padding-inline-end",
                "container.padding-inline-start-with-icon",
                "container.padding-inline-end-with-icon",
                "container.padding-block",
                "label.typescale",
                "icon.size",
                "icon.size-without-label",
                "container.gap",
                "outline.width",
                "motion.state-duration"
              ]
            },
            "variant": {
              "default": "filled",
              "from": "states"
            }
          }
        },
        "container": {
          "shape": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.shape.corner.full}",
            "$description": "The corners. Fully rounded in the default system: a button with a label is a pill, an icon-only button, which is as wide as it is high, a circle. A smaller corner draws a rounded rectangle and a rounded square."
          },
          "height": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "The container's height, per size, and the width of an icon-only button at its default width.",
            "small": {
              "$value": {
                "value": 32,
                "unit": "px"
              },
              "$extensions": {
                "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                  "fn": "mul",
                  "of": "{tanrei.sys.control.height.small}",
                  "by": 1,
                  "min": "{tanrei.sys.target.minimum}"
                }
              }
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": {
                "value": 40,
                "unit": "px"
              },
              "$extensions": {
                "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                  "fn": "mul",
                  "of": "{tanrei.sys.control.height.medium}",
                  "by": 1,
                  "min": "{tanrei.sys.target.minimum}"
                }
              }
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": {
                "value": 56,
                "unit": "px"
              },
              "$extensions": {
                "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                  "fn": "mul",
                  "of": "{tanrei.sys.control.height.large}",
                  "by": 1,
                  "min": "{tanrei.sys.target.minimum}"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "padding-inline-narrow": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "The inset on each side of the glyph of an icon-only button whose width is narrow, per size: the button is as wide as its glyph's box (icon.size-without-label) and this twice, and no wider (BTN-12). The default system holds it at 4 at every size, the least room that keeps a glyph clear of the capsule's edge; a narrow button is then 28, 32 and 32 wide. A system that wants its narrow buttons to differ more by size gives a size a larger value; it should not go below the default's. The hit area still meets the minimum target (BTN-5).",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
                "rationale": "One product packs icon actions tightly in one place (a dense toolbar, a row of a table) and gives one of them weight in another (the play button among transport controls), at the same height; the height alone cannot say both. How tight the tight form is, is room beside a glyph: a product that changes its glyph's size keeps that room without restating a width.",
                "since": "0.1.0"
              }
            },
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space50}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space50}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space50}"
            }
          },
          "width-wide": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "The width of an icon-only button whose width is wide, per size: about one and a quarter to one and a third of the height, for the action of a row that should weigh more or be easier to hit.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
                "rationale": "One product packs icon actions tightly in one place (a dense toolbar, a row of a table) and gives one of them weight in another (the play button among transport controls), at the same height; the height alone cannot say both.",
                "since": "0.1.0"
              }
            },
            "small": {
              "$value": {
                "value": 40,
                "unit": "px"
              },
              "$extensions": {
                "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                  "fn": "mul",
                  "of": "{tanrei.dial.size.unit}",
                  "by": 10
                }
              }
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": {
                "value": 52,
                "unit": "px"
              },
              "$extensions": {
                "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                  "fn": "mul",
                  "of": "{tanrei.dial.size.unit}",
                  "by": 13
                }
              }
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": {
                "value": 72,
                "unit": "px"
              },
              "$extensions": {
                "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                  "fn": "mul",
                  "of": "{tanrei.dial.size.unit}",
                  "by": 18
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "gap": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "Distance between the icon and the label, per size. The same at every size by default.",
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space100}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space100}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space100}"
            }
          },
          "padding-inline-start": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "Leading padding (start side in the reading direction).",
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space200}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space200}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space300}"
            }
          },
          "padding-inline-end": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space200}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space200}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space300}"
            }
          },
          "padding-inline-start-with-icon": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "Leading padding when the icon is at the leading side: a step tighter than padding-inline-start (4 less at small and medium, 8 less at large), as the main action button pads its icon's side, because a glyph carries empty space inside its box and the same padding as a label's reads as wider.",
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space150}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space150}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space200}"
            }
          },
          "padding-inline-end-with-icon": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "Trailing padding when the icon is at the trailing side, the mirror of padding-inline-start-with-icon and tighter than padding-inline-end by the same step.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
                "rationale": "One product puts the icon after the label on some buttons (Next →, an external link, a menu's chevron) and before it on others; a product that tightens the padding on the icon's side for a leading icon needs the same for a trailing one, or the two forms of one button are drawn out of balance.",
                "since": "0.1.0"
              }
            },
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space150}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space150}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space200}"
            }
          },
          "padding-block": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$description": "Vertical padding. Heights are minimums, so this only shows when the label wraps or text is enlarged.",
            "small": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space75}"
            },
            "medium": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space75}"
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.space.space75}"
            }
          }
        },
